# Chaos: streamer mode, cinema mode and the New Record auto screenshot (O411; client/BASE.md "0186";
# mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/misc.otui, options/screenshot.otui, src/client/creature.h, creature.cpp,
# luafunctions_client.cpp; after 0001-0185). The overlay modules client_chaos_streamer and game_chaosshots do the work.
#  * dataset.lua: `streamerMode`, `streamerHideSender`, `streamerHideOwnName`, `cinemaHideOthers` (all off); their apply
#    tells the global ChaosStreamer (`onOption(name, value)`). `screenshotRecord` (on): one more auto screenshot event.
#  * options/misc.otui: a panel after "Quick Login" with the four boxes (Options > Misc.).
#  * options/screenshot.otui: "New Record" under "Boss Defeated" (Options > Misc. > Screenshot); the panel has the room.
#  * C++: `Creature.setInfoHide(mask)` / `getInfoHide()` (static). Bit 1 leaves out the local player's name (plate, guild
#    and title lines too), bit 2 the name, bars and icons of every other player. 0 draws as before. The engine has one
#    switch for all names (UIMap.setDrawNames), so the per-creature rule needs this check in Creature::drawInformation.
# Without the patch: the modes still work from their hotkeys (saved in g_settings), without the two name rules; the
# New Record shot counts as on. Applies cleanly after 0001-0185; the C++ part not built here.
